  "executed": "The internal mesh asset ID for published Model 73559951039514 (\"Abandoned Warehouse 01\") is NOT obtainable without Roblox Studio. This is a definitive (B) finding.\n\nKey findings:\n1. The Open Cloud Assets API (apis.roblox.com/assets/v1/assets/73559951039514) returns metadata only (assetId, displayName, assetType, state, moderationState). It has NO download, export, content, file, children, meshes, or parts sub-endpoint. All such paths return 404.\n2. The Asset Delivery API (assetdelivery.roblox.com/v1/assetId/73559951039514) is the correct endpoint for downloading model content, but it requires Cookie (.ROBLOSECURITY) authentication per the official docs. Using x-api-key returns HTTP 200 with body {\"errors\":[{\"code\":403,\"message\":\"User is not authorized to access Asset.\"}]}. No .ROBLOSECURITY cookie exists in the keychain or environment.\n3. The asset.roblox.com domain does not resolve (DNS failure).\n4. The roblox-assets project (roblox_assets/publish/roblox.py) contains only upload code (POST /assets/v1/assets), no download code.\n5. The project .rbxmx file (abandoned_warehouse_interior_01.rbxmx) is a DIFFERENT asset (root model \"Sketchfab_Scene\", a Sketchfab import with 62 MeshParts), NOT the published Model 73559951039514. Its mesh IDs are irrelevant.\n6. The factory manifest (abandoned_warehouse_01/final/manifest.json) confirms the model was published from a GLB file (model_roblox_hq.glb) via the Open Cloud API. The .model.json shows IntegrationState: \"AwaitingModelImport\" with empty Children, confirming the model has never been imported into Studio.\n7. The internal mesh asset ID is assigned by Roblox's import pipeline when a Model is processed in Studio. It is not exposed via any API key-authenticated endpoint.\n\nTo obtain the mesh ID, the model must be imported into Roblox Studio (triggering the import pipeline), or the Asset Delivery API must be called with a valid .ROBLOSECURITY session cookie.\n",
